```roff
.TH hsh 1 "MAY 19, 2026" "1.0" "hsh (simple_shell) Man Page"

.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.I (No options included as of this writing)

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a custom implementation of a simple UNIX shell.
A minimalistic approach was taken in its design and implementation
to provide the basic functions of a shell similar to the one designed
by Ken Thompson. Design, compilation, and testing were conducted on
Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.

.SH OVERVIEW
Similar to other command line interfaces, the shell takes input
from either the terminal or scripts and executes them as they appear.

.SH INVOCATION
The GNU Compiler Collection,
.B gcc
, is recommended for compiling the shell with the following flags:

.P
.RS
.B gcc -Wall -Werror -Wextra -pedantic -std=gnu89 *.c -o hsh
.RE

.P
To start the shell in interactive mode:

.P
.RS
.B ./hsh
.br
#cisfun$ /bin/ls
.RE

.P
To run the shell in non-interactive mode:

.P
.RS
.B echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.RE

.SH FEATURES
The shell:
.IP \(bu 2
Displays a prompt in interactive mode
.IP \(bu 2
Reads user input using getline
.IP \(bu 2
Executes commands using fork and execve
.IP \(bu 2
Waits for child processes using wait
.IP \(bu 2
Handles commands with arguments

.SH BUILTINS
The following builtin commands are supported:

.TP
.B env
Prints all current environment variables.

.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The shell returns 0 on success.

.SH BUGS
No known bugs have been found or reported as of May 19, 2026.

